---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import DesktopPreview from '../components/DesktopPreview.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<SiteLayout page="features" title="Features — FlameWM" description="Discover the FlameWM design direction: familiar workflow, native Rust foundation, desktop controls, workspaces and thoughtfully simple settings.">
<section class="subhero"><div class="container subhero-inner" data-reveal><span class="eyebrow red">FEATURES / A MORE CONSIDERED DESKTOP</span><h1>Good design feels<br /><em>effortless.</em></h1><p>FlameWM aims to give you the comfort of a familiar desktop with the clarity and efficiency of a lightweight window manager.</p></div></section>
<section class="feature-deep"><div class="container deep-grid"><div data-reveal><span class="eyebrow red">01 / EVERYDAY WORK</span><h2>Right where you<br />expect it.</h2><p>Start menu, taskbar, workspaces, status controls and window actions in the places you already know. FlameWM is designed to feel familiar on day one.</p><div class="deep-bullets"><span>Application launcher and taskbar</span><span>Desktop files and workspace controls</span><span>Window snapping and multitasking</span></div></div><div class="deep-preview" data-reveal><DesktopPreview compact={true} /><small>Illustrative concept preview</small></div></div></section>
<section class="feature-deep feature-deep-alt"><div class="container deep-grid reversed"><div class="deep-image" data-reveal><img src={`${base}assets/images/flamewm-settings.webp`} alt="FlameWM settings reference showing About page and navigation" width="755" height="505" loading="lazy" /><small>Existing development screenshot</small></div><div data-reveal><span class="eyebrow red">02 / MEANINGFUL CONTROL</span><h2>Make it yours.<br />Keep it simple.</h2><p>Personalize the essentials through clear, direct settings. The interface focuses on real-world choices instead of exposing implementation details.</p><div class="deep-bullets"><span>Appearance and accent colors</span><span>Display and desktop settings</span><span>Keyboard shortcut preferences</span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="feature-deep"><div class="container deep-grid"><div data-reveal><span class="eyebrow red">03 / UNDER THE HOOD</span><h2>Built for the<br />lighter side.</h2><p>FlameWM is an independent Rust project drawing on the proven ideas of classic window managers. Its goal is a polished desktop with a small footprint and minimal background work.</p><div class="deep-bullets"><span>Rust implementation</span><span>Lightweight-first engineering decisions</span><span>Open development on GitHub</span></div></div><div class="engine-art" data-reveal><div class="engine-top">FLAMEWM / ARCHITECTURE</div><div class="engine-center"><div>YOUR WORKFLOW</div><span>↓</span><div>FLAMEWM DESKTOP</div><span>↓</span><div>RUST · NATIVE WINDOW MANAGEMENT</div></div><div class="engine-bottom">Purpose-built. Nothing extra.</div></div></div></section>
<section class="last-cta"><div class="container last-cta-inner" data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">EXPLORE THE DIRECTION</span><h2>See it in action.</h2><p>The browser demo is a design prototype, not an installable operating system.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-accent" href={`${base}try/`}>Try the prototype ↗</a><a class="button button-outline" href="https://github.com/ArkFlame/flamewm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Browse the source ↗</a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
